       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Doses are usually split as up to 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Risk:** At twice the maximum, the main concern is lactic acidosis. GI toxicity is also likely.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose, depending on the patient's current regimen\n\nPlease tell me which dose you intended, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate. If it is, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I'll enter the order once you confirm."
      }
